        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Incomplete sari, both ends intact but with side borders cut away in the middle. Black and white checked cotton field, pallu with broad horizontal bands of gold-wrapped thread and red silk; the other end with horizontal bands of white cotton and red silk. Both side borders of red silk with a narrow green stripe and gold-wrapped thread in triangle design."@en , "The complete object would have been intended for use as a garment, clothing."@en , "Textile, sari, woven cotton, silk and gold-wrapped thread, Central India, ca. 1867"@en ;
